// --- solo-unplayable CanPlay census ----------------------------------

/// Card identities `_card_can_play` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) refuses while the living
/// player count is one. The generated identity set is static; the Rust
/// play path evaluates this live condition against the admitted party.
/// The generator also parses `_apply_action_impl` and refuses unless
/// its application-time set is exactly this set plus `LARGESSE`. Python
/// deliberately offers Largesse through CanPlay, then refuses its solo
/// application, so Largesse does not belong in this CanPlay table.
///
/// **This is not `STOKE_POOL_EXCLUSIONS_V109["multiplayer_only"]`.**
/// That one is a five-member generation-pool exclusion set; this is the
/// playability census. They overlap on four names and disagree on the
/// rest, so reaching for the wrong one produces a plausible fix that
/// does not fix anything (#1613).
///
/// Python source condition: `len(_living_player_keys(s)) <= 1`.
