/// Each character pool's complete MEMBERSHIP, in native
/// `<Character>CardPool::GenerateAllCards` order.
///
/// This is `CardPoolModel::get_AllCardIds` (RVA `0x7e4dc` =
/// `get_AllCards().Select(Id).ToHashSet()`, and `get_AllCards`
/// RVA `0x7e4a6` is `GenerateAllCards`), which is the set
/// `CardModel::get_Pool` (RVA `0x7c878` IL_001b–IL_002d)
/// searches to answer WHICH POOL A CARD BELONGS TO. Nothing
/// is filtered: `Basic`, non-`CanBeGeneratedInCombat` and
/// `MultiplayerConstraint != None` rows are all members, and
/// `CardFactory::GetDefaultTransformationOptions` (RVA
/// `0x112960` IL_0041–IL_0047) reads `original.Pool` for
/// every non-Quest, non-`{Ancient, Event, Token}` original —
/// the generable/constraint/epoch predicates apply to the
/// CANDIDATES it then draws (`GetUnlockedCards` at
/// IL_005f, `GetFilteredTransformationOptions` RVA
/// `0x112a30` IL_005f–IL_0087 and IL_00a0–IL_00b6), never to
/// the original. Use `CHARACTER_CARD_POOL_ROWS_V1101` below
/// for candidates and this table for origins.
///
/// The generator proves these five and the Colorless pool are
/// pairwise disjoint, so the lookup does not depend on
/// `ModelDb.AllCardPools` order.
